			"description": "\"The issuer of a review invitation must be able to specify the maximum time allowed for the user to accept it. When this time expires, the review invitation is automatically cancelled by the system, and it becomes invisible for the invited user, but not for the user who created it.\"\n\n---\n\nThis folder executes the following workflow:\n\n- The Owner (User 1) invites User 6 to review the film \"Avatar\" via a POST request. During this action, User 1 specifies the deadline for the review invitation.\n    \n- User 6 logs in and performs a GET request to verify the presence of the pending invitation.\n    \n- To simulate an expired invitation, please open `databasev1.db` usin DB Browser. Open the `review` table and manually modify ONLY the `expirationDate` field to a past date (e.g. 2017-02-28T12:00:00.000Z). Click \"Write Changes\" to save.\n    \n- return to postman and log in again as user 6. if you repeat the GET request for pending invitations, the list will be empty because the previous invitation has been updated to \"expired\".\n    \n- However, if you log in as user 1 (owner) and repeat the get request, you will se the expired invitation, as required.\n    \n\n**Note:** To repeat this test, you must reset the database state manually. Open `databaseV1.db` with DB Browser, go to the `reviews` table, and execute this SQL query:\n\n`DELETE FROM reviews WHERE filmId = 3 and reviewerId = 6;`"
		},
