			"description": "\"The status of all the review invitations sent for a film, including their expiration time, must be visible, but only to the film owner who created those invitations. In particular, the film owner must be able to know if any review invitation is in the pending state, or if it has been accepted by the invited user, or if it is expired. To avoid the transfer of unnecessary information, the film owner should also have the option to select the information to retrieve (e.g. only invitations in the pending state, if any).\"\n\n---\n\nThis folder executes the following workflow:\n\n- The Owner (User 2) logs in and performs a GET request to view all sent review invitations. The response includes detailed status and expiration dates for each invitation.\n    \n- This data is visible only to the owner. For instance, if User 5 logs in and performs the same request, he will not see the invitation details (as per requirements).\n    \n- The owner can also filter invitations by status (accepted, pending, expired). If no invitations exist for a specific status, the server returns an empty array.\n    \n\nNOTE: to perform this test, the database is already populated with 1 review expired, 1 review accepted and 0 reviews pending."
		},
